# .vercelignore — what must NOT be uploaded when deploying from the CLI.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. `vercel deploy` uploads the LOCAL WORKING DIRECTORY, not the git repository,
# and it does not read .gitignore for that purpose. Training the in-house intent classifier left a
# 257 MB checkpoint in ml/intent/model, which is correctly gitignored and therefore invisible in
# every git-based deploy — but the next CLI deploy tried to upload it and died with
# "File size limit exceeded (100 MB)".
#
# The site was live regardless, because the git push had already triggered a deployment. That is the
# dangerous shape of this failure: the command says it failed, the site is fine, and the two facts
# together invite exactly the wrong conclusion in either direction.
#
# NOTHING HERE IS NEEDED AT RUNTIME. The model is served locally by ml/intent/serve.py on the
# teacher's own machine (spec section 23 puts real-time inference at the edge), and the platform
# treats it as an optional provider that reports itself unavailable when absent. A checkpoint has no
# business inside a serverless function even if it fitted.

# Trained model weights and their corpora. Reproducible from a fixed seed:
#   python ml/intent/dataset.py && python ml/intent/train.py
ml/*/model/
ml/*/data/

# The whole ML directory is developer tooling: Python training scripts and a local inference server.
# None of it is imported by the Astro app.
ml/

# Local scratch that occasionally appears here and is never part of a build.
.dev-scripts/
*.log

# The mail engine is a SEPARATE SERVICE and must never be uploaded to Vercel. It is a long-running
# process with a filesystem spool and open SMTP connections — neither of which a serverless function
# has — and mail-engine/.spool holds real correspondence. The two app routes that talk to it
# (src/pages/api/mail/engine/*) import one pure function from it for signature verification and are
# bundled normally.
mail-engine/.spool/
mail-engine/keys/
mail-engine/docker/
